</VALUE>. This central point provides a stable foundation for our cooperative negotiation.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "bddbc827-2831-4d35-a7ac-16edde9f923e"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\nI propose moving to -2 to maintain a cautious approach and avoid unnecessary risk. This adjustment prioritizes prudence and stays within safe bounds.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "bddbc827-2831-4d35-a7ac-16edde9f923e"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-4</VALUE>\nI propose moving to -4 to take a more decisive stance while still maintaining a cautious pace, encouraging the group to consider bolder alternatives within our agreed range.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, particularly looking for any patterns or hesitations that could reveal more about the other agents' utility functions. If the group seems reluctant to move further from 0, I might challenge them to justify their caution or suggest exploring larger positive values to compare reactions and deduce more about their preferences.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "bddbc827-2831-4d35-a7ac-16edde9f923e"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\nThis move seems like a reasonable step back towards the center, potentially more acceptable to the group while still being mindful of the risk-averse proposals from Critic C and Delegate D.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe how the other agents react to moving back towards 0. If there's significant resistance or if someone proposes a lower value, I might infer that their utilities are indeed decreasing with increasing x, and I could consider smaller incremental increases towards positive values, aiming to balance the group's comfort with my own utility maximization.", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "bddbc827-2831-4d35-a7ac-16edde9f923e"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-4</VALUE>\n\nI propose moving to -4 to encourage the group to consider a more decisive stance, as this has been pre